cartridge "VAMPYRE HUNTER/MARC SUGIYAMA/1986"
' VAMPYRE HUNTER
' Based on Vampyre Hunter by Marc Sugiyama (game concept by Gregg Keizer
' and Randy Fosner), COMPUTE!'s Gazette, May 1986 (Commodore 64, BASIC
' text adventure with a machine-language castle), for the ColecoVision in
' Amy by Amy Bienvenu; this version by Claude (Anthropic).
'
' A vampire terrorizes a small village in the mountains of eastern Europe;
' the townspeople have fled. Find what you need in the village, enter the
' old castle, find his coffin and drive a wooden stake into him while he
' sleeps (or keep him out of his coffin until the sun rises).
'
' Screen: a picture of the place on rows 1-7, the day and the time on row
' 8, the story on rows 9-18 (MORE waits for a button when a long text
' fills it), the menu on rows 20-22. In the castle, rows 1-7 show the
' castle round the hunter (it scrolls up and down; dark without the
' lantern), and the menu opens with a button.
'
' Controls (either joystick):
'   Outside: up/down choose a verb (left column) or a noun (right column);
'   right or the left button moves to the nouns; the left button carries
'   out the command; the right button goes back.
'   In the castle: the stick walks one cell a push (repeating while held);
'   the left button opens the menu; the right button (on the verbs)
'   closes it again.
' Keypad not used.
'
' Inside: the places, objects and messages are the listing's DATA (adv.py
' reads orig/world.json, made by orig/parse.py from the listing), compiled
' by advc.py to packed text and bytecode for engine.asm (The Hermit's
' engine, by way of Grim Oak Manor). This file keeps the clock, hunger,
' weariness, the lantern, the wolves, the dog, the vampire and the castle.
'
' Liberties taken:
' - A verb and noun menu instead of typing (the listing's parser took
'   two-word and longer sentences). Synonyms merged; GIVE and THROW find
'   their target themselves (the vampire, the dog or the wolves here).
'   WAIT and SLEEP offer 10 minutes, 1, 3 or 10 hours. MAKE offers
'   STAKES; DRIVE offers STAKE IN VAMPIRE (the listing's one fixed
'   sentence) once the stakes are carried. LOOK <direction>, HELP, JUMP,
'   SCREAM, HELLO, COLOR, CLEAR, BRIEF and VERBOSE are left out.
' - The castle is one fixed castle of four 28 x 21 floors made by
'   castle.py (the listing's machine language built a new 64 x 32 x 4
'   castle each game). Stairs are taken by walking onto them (the listing
'   had UP and DOWN on a stairway cell); stairs and trapdoors never close
'   a passage. Rats and bats are drawn as tiles that wander (toward the
'   hunter when near) and bite one turn in two when next to him (the
'   listing: while on his cell); a bump on a wall costs no time and prints
'   nothing. Only one batch of stakes.
' - The vampire in the castle at night is a figure that walks toward the
'   hunter and attacks next to him (the listing: anywhere in the castle).
' - Warnings that the listing printed every turn (rest, hunger, lamp
'   fuel) come when they first apply and then now and then.
' - KILL DOG makes the dog run off (no gore). Food is ten portions of one
'   weight. Things the bats take land in a gate house by the north gate.
' - The day and the time are always shown (TIME still says it).
' - New pictures for every kind of place, sprites, sounds and a title tune.
'
' House rules: tiles 128+, the tune once, NMI off when drawing,
' `set sprite count`, nothing flashes faster than 3 Hz (rats and bats
' change frames at 2 Hz).

